  "details": "<p>The Barrington Atlas Directory notes: at Bard, SE Vitricium</p>\r\n<p>The chronology of the Ponte di Bard is uncertain. Its origins may lie in the Roman period, but it is not mentioned until 1272 in the<span>\u00a0</span><i>Computa della Castellania di Bard</i><span>, which is preserved in the state archives in Turin\u00a0 (l'</span><a href=\"https://it.wikipedia.org/wiki/Archivio_di_Stato_di_Torino\" title=\"Archivio di Stato di Torino\">Archivio di Stato di Torino</a>).<span><br /></span></p>",
  "review_state": "published",
  "type": "FeatureCollection",
  "description": "The so-called \"Ponte di Bard\" located at Bard, to the southeast of Vitricium.",
